description:
FILED + FIXED s532c (Opus agent, 2026-11-06): the reduction of #4221 (Mojo-DOM58 t/dom.t 'Tap into method chain' / 'Nodes' / "Not an ARRAY reference").

    package O;
    sub new { my ($c, $t) = @_; bless { t => $t }, $c }
    sub tree { $_[0]{t} }
    sub other   { return "root" if (my $tree = ['fresh'])->[0] eq 'root'; return $tree->[0] }
    sub replace { my ($self) = @_;
                  return "parsed" if (my $tree = $self->tree)->[0] eq 'root';
                  my $before = $tree->[0]; my $o = $self->other;
                  return "before=$before after=$tree->[0] other=$o" }
    package main; print O->new(['tag'])->replace, "\n";

  perl 5.40.3: before=tag after=tag other=fresh.   PCL (ce665621): before=tag after=fresh other=fresh.

MECHANISM: the embedded-`my` arm (`_blk_expr`: let-bind fresh containers around the statement and the block remainder) took only Pl::Stmt's `plain` statements (exactly PPI::Statement / ::Expression); a `return` / `next` / `last` is a PPI::Statement::Break, Pl::Stmt kind `return` / `loopctl`, lowered by `_blk_tail` -- no let, so `(my $tree = ...)` lowered to `(p-scalar-= $tree ...)` on the forward-declared package cell.  Mojo::DOM58 spells `return ... if (my $tree = $self->tree)->[0] eq 'root'` in `parent` / `replace` and more; `replace`'s `_nodes($self->_parse($new))` argument ran a second such sub and overwrote the node `_replace` then searched for, so `->remove` spliced nothing.

FIX (s532c): Pl::Stmt gives return / loopctl records `plain => 1`; Parser2's %BLOCK_ARM routes both kinds through `_blk_expr` (its non-embedded path is `_blk_tail`, unchanged); the two other readers of "a plain statement declares at its block level" agree -- `_embedded_decl_candidates` (the promoter) and `_stmt_declares_canon` (the scope walk).  The binder already read the `my` token-wise.  Guard `Pl/t/modifier-my-01.t` (FAILS on ce665621).
